{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5","id":1502344,"title":"Gnosis being removed / being relegated to Renown in W5","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-06T21:51:19-08:00","id":1502344,"title":"Gnosis being removed / being relegated to Renown in W5","content":"no... just... no.<br /> <br /> Who the hell thought this was a good idea?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T22:07:28-08:00","id":1502345,"title":"","content":"I assume that question is rhetorical...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T22:51:10-08:00","id":1502348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5#post1502344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">no... just... no.<br /> <br /> Who the hell thought this was a good idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>Where did that info come from?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T00:28:45-08:00","id":1502353,"title":"","content":"The W5 QA<br /> <br /> It's actually been said in it since you first posted it. I myself didn't even notice it until it was pointed out in a reddit thread:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf 5 Q&amp;A</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Can you say anything about how gnosis will be handled including if it exists?</b><br /> <br /> Gnosis as a concept isn't present in W5, and the function it previously had is subsumed by Renown and a few other systems (some Gifts cost Rage or Willpower, for example).</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf 5 Q&amp;A</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Is Gnosis still a thing, renamed or otherwise, and if so how does it work in the new edition?</b><br /> <br /> The functions of Gnosis are largely replaced by Renown, in the interest of fewer trackers, stat-bookkeeping, and streamlining.</div> </div> </div> </div>This edition of Werewolf is going to be utterly horrible. Gnosis was NEVER a problem for me to track. The only oWoD game where it was definitely hard to keep track of all your &quot;energy&quot; stat blocks, was Mummy. KotE a little bit, but with practice, you'd get the hang of keeping track of Yin and Yang.<br /> <br /> There is no reason why Gnosis should be removed at all, other than the fact they want to de-emphasize the Umbra and make the game more like Forsaken.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 02-07-2023, 04:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T00:36:26-08:00","id":1502354,"title":"","content":"I guess they figured having 3 types of energy (Rage, Willpower and Gnosis) was too difficult for their audience to be able to keep track of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T01:07:47-08:00","id":1502358,"title":"","content":"Gnosis is as intrinsic to the Garou as Rage is.. there is legitimately no good faith reason on why it should've been removed at all. I highly doubt &quot;3 types of energy&quot; was their true motive of removing it. I'm just floored at how Paradox is just destroying every gameline now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T01:18:13-08:00","id":1502359,"title":"","content":"It could have been painfully easy to rename Gnosis (because the name does make zero sense) and then have it be something like Humanity where you measure your distance from the ideals of Gaia via Stains/Taint. Instead of a power pool which WoD5 hates so much, make it a stress meter from going into battle and needing to decompress or something.<br /> <br /> Sometimes it seriously feels like they're not even trying to make these things work. If you want to play up the isolation and alienation of being a werewolf... there was a perfectly good way to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T01:31:06-08:00","id":1502361,"title":"","content":"Rage was already a way that set up isolation and alienation in Werewolves from humans. The more Rage you had, and the lower the Willpower of some of the humans around you, they would fear and try to stay away from you. And that's where Kinfolk came to be important, to act as an interface toward human society. Forging a family due those factors were important. <br /> <br /> They don't feel the need to try, because Paradox ultimately doesn't really care about oWoD. The way they've designed V5, H5, and now W5 just plainly shows that. They want it to make it identical to CofD with the branding of oWoD. And ironically, Paradox doesn't care about CofD or its community, because they should know that CofD players don't want a reskinned CofD of their games. They just want CofD editions to continue their development.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T01:31:58-08:00","id":1502362,"title":"","content":"Gaia wept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T01:32:00-08:00","id":1502363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502353#post1502353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The W5 QA<br /> There is no reason why Gnosis should be removed at all, utter than the fact they want to de-emphasize the Umbra and make the game more like Forsaken.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, not even like Forsaken. Forsaken still have their essence. No, this is making any spiritual stuff solely the job of the ST.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T03:38:32-08:00","id":1502371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502359#post1502359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could have been painfully easy to rename Gnosis (because the name does make zero sense) and then have it be something like Humanity where you measure your distance from the ideals of Gaia via Stains/Taint. Instead of a power pool which WoD5 hates so much, make it a stress meter from going into battle and needing to decompress or something.<br /> <br /> Sometimes it seriously feels like they're not even trying to make these things work. If you want to play up the isolation and alienation of being a werewolf... there was a perfectly good way to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or just standardize it with Spirits and call it Essence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T03:47:34-08:00","id":1502374,"title":"","content":"Essence comes from all three stats though right? <br /> <br /> I don't know why they're so deadset at trying to make the worst possible decisions at every level? The term Gnosis even had some interesting thematic implications: knowledge detaching you from reality and such being an interesting counterweight to Rage, your instinctual reaction to control a reality gone wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T03:58:53-08:00","id":1502375,"title":"","content":"Also, why does using Gifts involve spending Willpower or Rage? On the <a href=\"https://www.worldofdarkness.com/news/werewolf-the-apocalypse-tribes-and-renown\" target=\"_blank\">dev-blog</a>, it was described as:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As well, Patron Spirits grant the ability for Garou to use their Gifts, spiritual powers that represent the Patron Spirit\u2019s goals and acumen. Most of these Gifts are taught by spirits that have something in common with the Patron Spirit, or might even be avatars of them. Whatever the case, invoking Gifts is effectively asking a spirit to intervene on one\u2019s behalf. And doing that requires the spirits to respect the Garou and their aims. </div> </div> </div>That explains why Renown is relevant but where is the idea of spending Rage/Willpower coming from if that's how Gifts work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T04:31:16-08:00","id":1502376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502371#post1502371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or just standardize it with Spirits and call it Essence?</div> </div> </div> </div>If we're talking about pre-W5? Sure why not. With W5, as we have no idea how the spirit rules are going to work (assuming there really are any) it would be a pretty big assumption that this would work cleanly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502374#post1502374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The term Gnosis even had some interesting thematic implications: knowledge detaching you from reality and such being an interesting counterweight to Rage, your instinctual reaction to control a reality gone wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem thematically is that it doesn't really work that way.<br /> <br /> If we're just talking about the Greek word &quot;gnosis&quot; than it doesn't inherently mean that. In fact quite the opposite it refers to something a kin to sapience or cognizance: the kind of abstract higher order thinking and intelligence that humans think separates humans from the rest of the animal world. That might be a counterpoint to Rage, but it doesn't reflect the rest of what Gnosis does as a game trait.<br /> <br /> If we're specifically using Gnosticism, it doesn't fit because WtA isn't a Gnostic themed game. The Garou don't transcend the base physical world through deep transcendental cultivation of divine knowledge. They're inherently part of a spirit world. Nothing Gnosis actually does in the game connects to the idea of enlightenment posed in Gnostic practices.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502375#post1502375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, why does using Gifts involve spending Willpower or Rage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wild speculation of how they'll explain it if they do? It's a demonstration of the Garou's dedication to their aim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T05:53:51-08:00","id":1502381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502353#post1502353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This edition of Werewolf is going to be utterly horrible. Gnosis was NEVER a problem for me to track. The only oWoD game where it was definitely hard to keep track of all your &quot;energy&quot; stat blocks, was Mummy. KotE a little bit, but with practice, you'd get the hang of keeping track of Yin and Yang.<br /> <br /> There is no reason why Gnosis should be removed at all, other than the fact they want to de-emphasize the Umbra and make the game more like Forsaken.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#cc0000\"><b>Please no Edition Warring before there's an Edition.</b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T08:17:28-08:00","id":1502393,"title":"","content":"I mean, the idea of Renown taking over from Gnosis and this giving Garou renown pools would be an interesting change, it's probably where Forsaken would have gone if it was further down the line of CofD Games. I mean, it's not what they're doing, and goes directly against the likely reasons they've removed Gnosis, but it would have been interesting. It would have changed Gifts into throwing your name around to get favours from Spirits.<br /> <br /> Also I have to concur that this isn't Forsaken. It's some bizarre proto-Forsaken missing the deep spiritual side of the Uratha or the reasons people might want to play it over Apocalypse. But I suppose any game will look like that when you're missing 90% of it. If anything I'll be somewhat happy if W5 comes out and it's actually gone in the exact opposite direction to Forsaken (which might be supported by Kin apparently being random occurrences with nothing special before the change while Wolf-Blooded have understood origins with legit supernatural benefits).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T12:58:10-08:00","id":1502416,"title":"","content":"The thing with Renown taking the place of Gnosis is that I feel it clashes with some of the changes W5 has made. The Garou-Nation has been torn apart, the Get of Fenris have been lost to Rage and Gaia's dead/dying... The flaws/problems of what Garou are and have done in the past are very obvious in this setup. And yet by making Renown a power-stat, the social construct of what is considered &quot;honorable&quot;, &quot;wise&quot; and &quot;glorious&quot; by Garou-culture are given an even more prominent position. After all, if player-characters are supposed to earn more Renown and be rewarded for doing that, why are the older Garou who already have a lot of Renown the idiots who let things get so bad...? Either earning Renown is a guide to Garou becoming deservedly more powerful or it isn't. You can't have &quot;The Garou-Nation has failed.&quot;, &quot;The Get's fall shows that being angry warriors is bad.&quot; and &quot;The failings of older Garou have gotten us into the middle of the Apocalypse.&quot; on one side and on the other tell players &quot;But you still gotta earn Renown in the eyes of your peers and the spirits in the same manner it has been done since the dawn of time.&quot;. This setup is strange because the flaws of Garou are way more obvious while the new system gives even more credence to Renown (and trying to earn it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T13:05:01-08:00","id":1502417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502416#post1502416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing with Renown taking the place of Gnosis is that I feel it clashes with some of the changes W5 has made. The Garou-Nation has been torn apart, the Get of Fenris have been lost to Rage and Gaia's dead/dying... The flaws/problems of what Garou are and have done in the past are very obvious in this setup. And yet by making Renown a power-stat, the social construct of what is considered &quot;honorable&quot;, &quot;wise&quot; and &quot;glorious&quot; by Garou-culture are given an even more prominent position. After all, if player-characters are supposed to earn more Renown and be rewarded for doing that, why are the older Garou who already have a lot of Renown the idiots who let things get so bad...? Either earning Renown is a guide to Garou becoming deservedly more powerful or it isn't. You can't have &quot;The Garou-Nation has failed.&quot;, &quot;The Get's fall shows that being angry warriors is bad.&quot; and &quot;The failings of older Garou have gotten us into the middle of the Apocalypse.&quot; on one side and on the other tell players &quot;But you still gotta earn Renown in the eyes of your peers and the spirits in the same manner it has been done since the dawn of time.&quot;. This setup is strange because the flaws of Garou are way more obvious while the new system gives even more credence to Renown (and trying to earn it).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, but you should not earn TOO MUCH renown. Only enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T13:11:37-08:00","id":1502418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502417#post1502417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, but you should not earn TOO MUCH renown. Only enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, Garou are very community-oriented... but don't get too many in one spot or it becomes a Rage-trigger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T13:19:01-08:00","id":1502419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502418#post1502418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, Garou are very community-oriented... but don't get too many in one spot or it becomes a Rage-trigger.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, so best way to be a W5 garou? Weekend warrior!<br /> <br /> I just want to be clear that I do not want to joke about this. I rather have W5 be a nice reboot than this. These jokes come from the feeling of confusion about the actual play of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T13:23:53-08:00","id":1502420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502419#post1502419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh yes, so best way to be a W5 garou? Weekend warrior!<br /> <br /> I just want to be clear that I do not want to joke about this. I rather have W5 be a nice reboot than this. These jokes come from the feeling of confusion about the actual play of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Either that ship's sailed, or they've been perplexingly awful at communicating intent and content of the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T13:32:29-08:00","id":1502421,"title":"","content":"I think it's not that too many garou in one place magically makes them more filled with Rage,it's that rites and other fragile and easy to break things are always in risk of being disturbed by one individual garou with rage","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 02-07-2023, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T13:43:29-08:00","id":1502425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502421#post1502421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's not that too many garou in one place magically makes them more filled with Rage,it's that rites and other fragile and easy to break things are always in risk of being disturbed by one individual garou with rage</div> </div> </div> </div>So they'll be occupied trying to keep the caern's spirits from angering way more often than before? No wonder they can't get out to do anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T13:46:05-08:00","id":1502426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502425#post1502425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So they'll be occupied trying to keep the caern's spirits from angering way more often than before? No wonder they can't get out to do anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>from what i've understood from the dev's comments it's more that make an Rite is a delicate precise process which means at least some of the garou involved have to be fine,and potentially one lonely Rage filled wolf can ruint","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T13:47:25-08:00","id":1502427,"title":"","content":"i didn't know gnosis was so important, i imagine you folks won't buy the corebook,but i'll do it and tell you all my thoughts on it on the forum,ok?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 02-07-2023, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T13:47:51-08:00","id":1502428,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it was in the context of Rites but even so... Justin Achilli even says that Rites get easier the more Garou participate. And yet...<br /> <br /> So are Garou not supposed to do Rites together when too many are in the same place? That's the complete opposite of being communal. How was there a Garou-Nation in the first place if Rage is this disruptive?<br /> <br /> Of course, looking at it from another direction, it's a way to make sure the game remains street-level and doesn't stray into epic storytelling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T13:52:14-08:00","id":1502430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502428#post1502428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it was in the context of Rites but even so... Justin Achilli even says that Rites get easier the more Garou participate. And yet...<br /> <br /> So are Garou not supposed to do Rites together when too many are in the same place? That's the complete opposite of being communal. How was there a Garou-Nation in the first place if Rage is this disruptive?<br /> <br /> Of course, looking at it from another direction, it's a way to make sure the game remains street-level and doesn't stray into epic storytelling.</div> </div> </div> </div>well it could just have been a an example he came up on the spot from the ama sessions,it might not be a comon re occurence","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T13:52:23-08:00","id":1502431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502427#post1502427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i didn't know gnosis was so important, i imagine you gellas won't buy the corebook,but i'll do it and tell you all my thoughts on it on the forum,ok?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a defined connection to the spirit world. Garou literally had a ritual hunt to replenish it as a connection to Gaia (the Sacred Hunt, which typically had a sept chasing after an engling-spirit). So, yeah, taking that out and having the reputation scoreboard take its place? Pretty weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T13:53:07-08:00","id":1502432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502431#post1502431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was a defined connection to the spirit world. Garou literally had a ritual hunt to replenish it as a connection to Gaia (the Sacred Hunt, which typically had a sept chasing after an engling-spirit). So, yeah, taking that out and having the reputation scoreboard take its place? Pretty weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>i thought gnosis was inner peace,an oppposite of Rage,my bad","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T13:58:11-08:00","id":1502433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502432#post1502432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i thought gnosis was inner peace,an oppposite of Rage,my bad</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, because of the connection to Gaia and the other half of existence that it represented. There might be ways to not need that to be a mechanically-expressed value in the game, but what W5 is doing? Not really feeling like it's one of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T14:29:26-08:00","id":1502438,"title":"","content":"I suspect that W5 is going to have an 'ideal pack/caern' size where having more Garou around makes Rites easier, but only until like 10 or 15. Then during the Rite everybody has to make a roll to avoid murder-rage.<br /> <br /> At least it's different to Forsaken, where the big theming of rites is based around the Uratha religion and pack (whereas in legacy WtA it was about community in a broader sense). I'm not sure it's a good difference, but it's there.<br /> <br /> I feel like the 'too many Garou=murder rage' thing is meant to mimic the Uratha dynamic of competing packs without getting why that was a natural result. Which really sums up the W5 previews, it wants to hammer in the what without going too deep into the why. Lobbyists are causing bad things, so let's make an evil spirit-possessed lobbyist antagonist! What do you mean that having the lobbyist be a human with explainable reasons might be more interesting and impactful? Garou work in small packs due to magic Rage reasons, not because being a network of semi-independent cells gives them a tactical advantage, or because they're prideful creatures competing over resources.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T15:01:50-08:00","id":1502444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502428#post1502428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, looking at it from another direction, it's a way to make sure the game remains street-level and doesn't stray into epic storytelling.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is with the obsession with street-level mechanics and themes, and why is there a need for everyone to be forced to play that way?<br /> <br /> &quot;Street-level&quot; doesn't even make sense for most Garou outside of the Bone Gnawers and Glass Walkers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T15:26:33-08:00","id":1502451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502444#post1502444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is with the obsession with street-level mechanics and themes, and why is there a need for everyone to be forced to play that way?<br /> <br /> &quot;Street-level&quot; doesn't even make sense for most Garou outside of the Bone Gnawers and Glass Walkers.</div> </div> </div> </div>i suspect to some people and maybe to the devs,a globe trotting game of high stakes and epic storytelling doesn't feel like a monster movie game. i personally i'm on the fence","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T15:44:13-08:00","id":1502453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502451#post1502451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i suspect to some people and maybe to the devs,a globe trotting game of high stakes and epic storytelling doesn't feel like a monster movie game. i personally i'm on the fence</div> </div> </div> </div>And what WoD game is a &quot;monster movie game&quot; except Hunter: The Reckoning (either version)?<ul><li>Vampire is nothing like a vampire monster movie. It's not a game about Nosferatu, Dracula, Hammer Horror Dracula or anything similar.</li> <li>Werewolf is nothing like a werewolf monster movie. It's not a game about lunacy, loss of humanity and loss of self to a beast within</li> <li>Wraith is nothing like a ghost movie, because while &quot;a haunting&quot; might be a thing for a individual obsessed with a fetter, that's not what a Wraith game is about</li> <li>Mummy is not like mummy monster movies, it replaces ancient predatory kings of the dead with immortals trading favours or hunting monsters</li> <li>Mage is Everything Everywhere All At Once</li> <li>Changeling is not a monster movie - it's Neverending Story, Labyrinth and Dark Crystal all rolled up into one</li> </ul><br /> You want a monster movie game? That's the territory of Night's Black Agents and They Came From...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":".  Formatting 02-07-2023, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T16:20:58-08:00","id":1502457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502453#post1502453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And what WoD game is a &quot;monster movie game&quot; except Hunter: The Reckoning (either version)?<br /> <br /> Vampire is nothing like a vampire monster movie. It's not a game about Nosferatu, Dracula, Hammer Horror Dracula or anything similar.<br /> Werewolf is nothing like a werewolf monster movie. It's not a game about lunacy, loss of humanity and loss of self to a beast within<br /> Wraith is nothing like a ghost movie, because while &quot;a haunting&quot; might be a thing for a individual obsessed with a fetter, that's not what a Wraith game is about<br /> Mummy is not like mummy monster movies, it replaces ancient predatory kings of the dead with immortals trading favours or hunting monsters<br /> Mage is Everything Everywhere All At Once<br /> Changeling is not a monster movie - it's Neverending Story, Labyrinth and Dark Crystal all rolled up into one<br /> <br /> You want a monster movie game? That's the territory of Night's Black Agents and They Came From...</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah you gotta a point,i however will point that in my experience there is some people who are pleased with the focus on street level stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T16:28:15-08:00","id":1502460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502457#post1502457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> yeah you gotta a point,i however will point that in my experience there is some people who are pleased with the focus on street level stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what is a typical Werewolf chronicle about? It's about a holy place, no matter where it is or what it is. Around it have gathered generations of humans, spirits and possibly wolves. They have complex interactions provoking conflict and relationships. This place is usually a bit out of the way, but always impacted by the fact that humanity is encroaching on the world and is everywhere, heck the holy place can be in the middle of the City. The Average cast are young upstarts who need to prove themselves to the world by protecting this area, learning how to commune with the local spirits and fight off local threats. They rise up and learn more about their place in the world and how to survive against its dangers. How much more &quot;street&quot; do you need it to be?<br /> <br /> Just because you could play it differently and focus on personal quests of a small group of heroes that seek more unity and coordination doesn't mean that's the given direction of the game nor that it's the default assumption. The only thing that W5 does here is that it forces just one mode of play and says you're bad thinking about anything else. So people aren't complaining about support for <i>the default game mode of Werewolf</i>, they're complaining about taking anything else away and shooting it in the back of the head because someone didn't like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"l