s=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502460#post1502460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So what is a typical Werewolf chronicle about? It's about a holy place, no matter where it is or what it is. Around it have gathered generations of humans, spirits and possibly wolves. They have complex interactions provoking conflict and relationships. This place is usually a bit out of the way, but always impacted by the fact that humanity is encroaching on the world and is everywhere, heck the holy place can be in the middle of the City. The Average cast are young upstarts who need to prove themselves to the world by protecting this area, learning how to commune with the local spirits and fight off local threats. They rise up and learn more about their place in the world and how to survive against its dangers. How much more &quot;street&quot; do you need it to be?<br /> <br /> Just because you could play it differently and focus on personal quests of a small group of heroes that seek more unity and coordination doesn't mean that's the given direction of the game nor that it's the default assumption. The only thing that W5 does here is that it forces just one mode of play and says you're bad thinking about anything else. So people aren't complaining about support for <i>the default game mode of Werewolf</i>, they're complaining about taking anything else away and shooting it in the back of the head because someone didn't like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>it might not be as restrictive as all that,i'll check for myself","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T16:59:26-08:00","id":1502465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502444#post1502444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is with the obsession with street-level mechanics and themes, and why is there a need for everyone to be forced to play that way?<br /> <br /> &quot;Street-level&quot; doesn't even make sense for most Garou outside of the Bone Gnawers and Glass Walkers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even Bone Gnawers are punching more than a little above the weight class of typical street-level games, thanks to a number of factors. Even the High Ban can't really stop them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T17:28:37-08:00","id":1502467,"title":"","content":"And trivializing the Garou down to street level is silly, considering the whole point of Garou staying in mid-to-low developed <b>suburbs</b> or <b>rural</b> areas is trying to stay away from the masses of humans.<br /> <br /> It's the complete opposite of why Vampires need cities: outside of Kinfolk, the Garou have a hard time with human society due to their Rage... if they wanted to remove anything, for better &quot;street level play&quot;, Rage would make sense in removing (but I would NEVER want this for Apocalypse at all).<br /> <br /> Suburban or Rural areas as the main areas where Garou stay around make sense, as a means to more easily centralized all Kinfolk and Garou in one location; without any interruption from humans who aren't Kinfolk and mess with Garou society. The only tribes adept at tempering their Rage to some extent are the Bone Gnawers, Glass Walkers, and Children of Gaia.. but even they could have some flare-ups that might disturb humans.<br /> <br /> The Garou aren't meant to be heroes anyway. They're not really meant to make friends with humanity. They're fighters against the enemies of Gaia; at the forefront of that being the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> Lowering their power levels or mechanics to streel level, to cater toward myths/misrepresentations of the series, is a horrible way to destroy the gameline. Just because something is &quot;high-powered&quot;, &quot;globe-trotting&quot;, &quot;epic-storytelling&quot; doesn't mean it can't be taken seriously, nor does it suddenly make the game about &quot;trenchcoat wielding katana wielding capeshit hero characters&quot; (and even then, don't shoehorn one mechanical style of play to ensure those who want to play it that way, can't do that anymore...).<br /> <br /> Ironically, they make the game even more farcical and loose in theme by how their pulling all the brakes to unnaturally make it &quot;street level&quot;. It's just horrible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 02-07-2023, 08:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T18:09:27-08:00","id":1502471,"title":"","content":"Another point here is that if the majority of &quot;... of Darkness&quot; customers wanted to more to a far more street level oriented game?<br /> <br /> The &quot;new&quot; WoD wouldn't have struggled so much to get everyone to move over to it. We already saw what a heavier focus on street level stuff looks like with early CofD 1e. We saw how people reacted to it. By the time the CofD started to course correct and start building up modes of play that touch of wider scale things, it was too late to stop a lot of fan divisions or people just moving from WoD to something else.<br /> <br /> The WoD and the CofD have both always done better when they're more open games than not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T00:50:46-08:00","id":1502487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502376#post1502376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem thematically is that it doesn't really work that way.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You're overthinking it. The main point was knowledge tempering savagery. Gnostic ideas are nice and all but the main idea is that Garou don't frenzy so badly when they've got that very spiritual resource and Most Gnosis powers veered towards being more clever or defensive while most rage powers were about violence. Gnosis gave you a spiritual connection, easier access to the umbra, resistance towards certain powers, guided you away from attacking allies in a frenzy, the fact that you had more resources to give made paying spirits less of a big deal... I'm sure I read some fluff that said those with high gnosis ratings can see the spirit world bleeding into the material one but that should probably come with mechanics. It is the antithis of rage, and that made it interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T01:11:40-08:00","id":1502488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502444#post1502444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is with the obsession with street-level mechanics and themes, and why is there a need for everyone to be forced to play that way?<br /> <br /> &quot;Street-level&quot; doesn't even make sense for most Garou outside of the Bone Gnawers and Glass Walkers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> they percieve it as the ideal game and the truest depiction of wod. Partly due to its punk aesthetic.<br /> <br /> Theirs a lot to unpack on that but notably they don't even do street level games very well since a lot of stuff which features in street level life is deliberatly absent-ethnicity, and social background, large scale institutions, ambitions, material capital and so on. If anything w5 feels less 'street' since tribes are disconnected abstracts and kinfolk arnt a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 02-08-2023, 04:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T01:21:52-08:00","id":1502489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502451#post1502451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i suspect to some people and maybe to the devs,a globe trotting game of high stakes and epic storytelling doesn't feel like a monster movie game. i personally i'm on the fence</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol dracula spanned Europe and involved an epic battle in the carpathian mountains with a vampire lord.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T02:19:52-08:00","id":1502494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502471#post1502471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another point here is that if the majority of &quot;... of Darkness&quot; customers wanted to more to a far more street level oriented game?<br /> <br /> The &quot;new&quot; WoD wouldn't have struggled so much to get everyone to move over to it. We already saw what a heavier focus on street level stuff looks like with early CofD 1e. We saw how people reacted to it. By the time the CofD started to course correct and start building up modes of play that touch of wider scale things, it was too late to stop a lot of fan divisions or people just moving from WoD to something else.<br /> <br /> The WoD and the CofD have both always done better when they're more open games than not.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not like CofD1e was an abject failure, a lot of the backlash was more due to throwing out the old lore and tone for something relatively bland. CofD really came into its own around the time of Changeling and Hunter, which is where it solidified it's status as its own thing. But some of the more popular parts of CofD are still the street level bits, even if there's sometimes other reasons for that. Sure 2e is more gonzo than 1e was, but it never really left the street/city level established in 2004.<br /> <br /> WoD5 is, of course, even more 'street' than CofD, but I don't think that's the actual reason people dislike it. Elder vampires are still powerful, even if not to the same extremes, although their weaknesses could do with a toning down, and Driven aren't exactly much weaker than Imbued, or at least Imbued who haven't gone full solar. What's changed is the status quo, expected PC factions, and similar things, and it wasn't gradually like when the Camarilla overtook the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> W5 makes a big change to how the Garou fight and organise, and those are the things coming up more than the 'street level' stuff. Rage is suddenly bad, Garou aren't actually meant to actively fight the Wyrm, and I can finally play a Silver Fang anarchist punk rocker from Wakefield (which I'll do just as soon as I have the desire to,, expect it around 2358).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T02:57:26-08:00","id":1502496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502487#post1502487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're overthinking it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm overthinking that the word doesn't mean what you think it means? Or that the mechanics don't really support your assertions at all?<br /> <br /> Willpower does waaaaaaay more to be the &quot;anithesis of Rage&quot; than Gnosis does. Gnosis only stops you from hurting your pack in a Frenzy. Willpower actually reduces the likelihood of Frenzies and reduce the impact of Rage's downsides. Rage and Gnosis are only antitheses in the sense of &quot;you can't use them at the same time unless you've got that one Gift.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The main point was knowledge tempering savagery. </div> </div> </div>Which it doesn't do. You might be overthinking what's in the book instead of your fanon here. Remember lupus get Gnosis 5 to start, homids get Gnosis 1. How is that about knowledges vs savagery? Wolves aren't inherently more knowledgeable than humans (and gnosis specifically means the opposite of this dynamic)... so this doesn't make sense no matter how much you want to cherry pick and make a hyperbole of what the books say.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T03:19:45-08:00","id":1502497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502496#post1502496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Willpower does waaaaaaay more to be the &quot;anithesis of Rage&quot; than Gnosis does. Gnosis only stops you from hurting your pack in a Frenzy. Willpower actually reduces the likelihood of Frenzies and reduce the impact of Rage's downsides. Rage and Gnosis are only antitheses in the sense of &quot;you can't use them at the same time unless you've got that one Gift.&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No?<br /> Willpower is yourself. Your soul or whatever. Werewolves are half spirit. Or rather they're a soul + a spirit, and the spirit has these two halves. Or maybe on one half you've got Man with Body and Mind and on the otherhalf you've got Spirit with Rage and Gnosis. Unlike with vampires and the Beast, werewolves aren't supposed to have a wholly negative dark passenger with them for their will to stave off. Rather the Changing Breed spirit has both noble (Gnosis) and base (Rage) aspects that the will should ideally balance. Narratively, this is great because Werewolves are connected to and supposed to care about something much greater than themselves, while vampires aren't. Taking away that Gnosis makes werewolves just as base as vampires.<br /> <br /> Edit: post got Swallowed by BS spam detector. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 02-11-2023, 12:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T16:20:52-08:00","id":1502547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502494#post1502494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not like CofD1e was an abject failure, a lot of the backlash was more due to throwing out the old lore and tone for something relatively bland.</div> </div> </div> </div>And by a team that was largely influenced by... the same person leading the charge on using &quot;street&quot; the same exact way for what the plans for WoD5 is.<br /> <br /> You don't need to defend the CofD from me. If I had to pick on &quot;... of Darkness&quot; line that would get new books, I would toss the WoD in a heartbeat for the CofD. I'm talking about what the people responsible for W5 are doing (which includes repeating the exact same mistakes from early CofD 1e).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T16:50:00-08:00","id":1502548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502547#post1502547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And by a team that was largely influenced by... the same person leading the charge on using &quot;street&quot; the same exact way for what the plans for WoD5 is.<br /> <br /> You don't need to defend the CofD from me. If I had to pick on &quot;... of Darkness&quot; line that would get new books, I would toss the WoD in a heartbeat for the CofD. I'm talking about what the people responsible for W5 are doing (which includes repeating the exact same mistakes from early CofD 1e).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but there's a lot of railing against the 'street level' idea both here and the QA thread, and it really bugs me. Because I'm about 90% certain that what people dislike isn't the street level stuff, it's the monofocus Justin is bringing along with it. A H2 where you could only play high ranking members of the SI who went out field agents would have been much less street, and just as disliked.<br /> <br /> The street level thing wasn't an issue with early CofD1e, partially because CofD2e still operates at that thematic level. It just ditched a LOT of the stuff that was combined with it but didn't actually need to be (notably a reduction in power level), and maintains enough comparability with 1e that there's still a LOT of options for groups. Partially I put that down to the designers of CofD2e actually being able to write a competent ruleset, unlike this JA fellow.<br /> <br /> W5 is in a really good position where it could feasibly bring the focus down while keeping the majority of the old lore. It's not doing that, it's throwing the existing lore about the Garou Nation and Umbra under a bus and replacing it with very little.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T20:41:16-08:00","id":1502578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502548#post1502548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but there's a lot of railing against the 'street level' idea both here and the QA thread, and it really bugs me. Because I'm about 90% certain that what people dislike isn't the street level stuff, it's the monofocus Justin is bringing along with it. A H2 where you could only play high ranking members of the SI who went out field agents would have been much less street, and just as disliked.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't anyone is saying street is in itself bad, it is the monofocus that is the issue. When I think back to when NWoD was released, I don't remember anyone complaining about the limited focus. It was the replacing of oWoD that was the problem.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T20:50:16-08:00","id":1502580,"title":"","content":"It's also how the designers (then and now) were talking - including the use of the word street - to describe the motivations for certain decisions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T01:13:33-08:00","id":1502594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502578#post1502578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't anyone is saying street is in itself bad, it is the monofocus that is the issue. When I think back to when NWoD was released, I don't remember anyone complaining about the limited focus. It was the replacing of oWoD that was the problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember at the time their was an idea in nwod advocates that you couldn't compare it to owod. An absurd notion since it explicitly replaced owod and borrowed heavily from it.<br /> I recall the reductive nature the setting initially did hurt it a lot. Especially with mage, it certainly had a 'you should be playing street ' vibe but was far less obnoxious about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 02-09-2023, 04:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T12:22:08-08:00","id":1502623,"title":"","content":"The focus on street wouldn't be so bad but for whatever reason, Justin Achilli (both with H5 and the W5 previews) immediately turned it into a point of contention. It would have been completely fine for H5 to have been a game about local hunter-cells and have that be the focus - but instead hunter-orgs are also demonized from top to bottom. If you're looking at the monster-hunter-genre or just the idea of stories where normal people deal with supernatural stuff and what sort of fiction people might associate with that, it's very strange to start out with the premise of &quot;Every hunter working for an organization isn't a true hunter.&quot;. And with W5 there's a similar feeling, isn't there? After all, you could make a WtA with a street-level-focus and avoid the more epic stuff. Okay, we already have WtF doing something along those lines but still... Why does the game focused on the local level have to be mid-Apocalypse then? If the game isn't about fighting an epic war to save Gaia why is Gaia being dead/dying part of the premise...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T12:34:58-08:00","id":1502626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502623#post1502623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The focus on street wouldn't be so bad but for whatever reason, Justin Achilli (both with H5 and the W5 previews) immediately turned it into a point of contention. It would have been completely fine for H5 to have been a game about local hunter-cells and have that be the focus - but instead hunter-orgs are also demonized from top to bottom. If you're looking at the monster-hunter-genre or just the idea of stories where normal people deal with supernatural stuff and what sort of fiction people might associate with that, it's very strange to start out with the premise of &quot;Every hunter working for an organization isn't a true hunter.&quot;. And with W5 there's a similar feeling, isn't there? After all, you could make a WtA with a street-level-focus and avoid the more epic stuff. Okay, we already have WtF doing something along those lines but still... <b>Why does the game focused on the local level have to be mid-Apocalypse then? If the game isn't about fighting an epic war to save Gaia why is Gaia being dead/dying part of the premise...?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm envisioning the DBZA version of Gohan's tutor, but instead of yelling &quot;Learn!&quot; when he whips Gohan, it's &quot;Angst! Angst! Angst! Are you feeling the angst yet?&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-10T14:10:02-08:00","id":1502709,"title":"","content":"I mean, if we presume Gaia's death is inevitable what's the point in fighting to save her? Why should you fight, why should you join the Get in their crusade, when it's been decided better to hunker down and wait until you can potentially rebuild.<br /> <br /> Of course, that really isn't any different to W1, but the Garou still fought. The Forsaken in WtF have a monumental task that they will inevitably fail at in the end, but they still fight. Because you can still get something out of an impossible or meaningless goal. At the very least creatures of rage who see their patron die should want to punch the perpetrators in the face.<br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> The thing that makes it hard to sympathise with the demonisation of the Get is that the exact moment they decided to fight harder is the moment the others abandoned them. They didn't try to reign the Get in, convince them there was a better way to fight, or offer to support, they seem to have gone 'lol, ur crazy, Gaia is dead, stop fighting'.<br /> <br /> I don't think whoever came up with the 'Gaia is dead' idea really thought through how a culture such as the Garou would react to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-10T15:13:11-08:00","id":1502712,"title":"","content":"If we're to take the contempt that JA had for W:tA at face value, considering it was never in the cards, and having them just collapse in defeat was always the plan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-10T15:26:03-08:00","id":1502713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502709#post1502709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, if we presume Gaia's death is inevitable what's the point in fighting to save her? Why should you fight, why should you join the Get in their crusade, when it's been decided better to hunker down and wait until you can potentially rebuild.<br /> <br /> Of course, that really isn't any different to W1, but the Garou still fought. The Forsaken in WtF have a monumental task that they will inevitably fail at in the end, but they still fight. Because you can still get something out of an impossible or meaningless goal. At the very least creatures of rage who see their patron die should want to punch the perpetrators in the face.<br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> The thing that makes it hard to sympathise with the demonisation of the Get is that the exact moment they decided to fight harder is the moment the others abandoned them. They didn't try to reign the Get in, convince them there was a better way to fight, or offer to support, they seem to have gone 'lol, ur crazy, Gaia is dead, stop fighting'.<br /> <br /> I don't think whoever came up with the 'Gaia is dead' idea really thought through how a culture such as the Garou would react to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's one question to pose in response to that: If those are so important to W5, why haven't we heard about them till now? And I think we haven't because the worldbuilding you'd need to answer questions like that isn't part of W5.<br /> <br /> And the Get of Fenris are the bad guys because they exactly act like the warrior-Garou desperately trying to save Gaia you'd imagine. And Garou-culture is bad, though. And so they're a warning symbol to all other werewolves.<br /> <br /> Of course, the players are still supposed to fight the Wyrm and fight the good fight to save Gaia.<br /> <br /> And it doesn't have to make sense, of course. Does the local hunter cell / hunter org - division make sense after all? Is really everyone working for a hunter-organisation evil...? Or in the context of W5: Is everybody who wants to fight to save Gaia evil...?<br /> <br /> H5 didn't make sense, so why should W5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-10T15:30:23-08:00","id":1502714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502709#post1502709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, if we presume Gaia's death is inevitable what's the point in fighting to save her? Why should you fight, why should you join the Get in their crusade, when it's been decided better to hunker down and wait until you can potentially rebuild.<br /> <br /> Of course, that really isn't any different to W1, but the Garou still fought. The Forsaken in WtF have a monumental task that they will inevitably fail at in the end, but they still fight. Because you can still get something out of an impossible or meaningless goal. At the very least creatures of rage who see their patron die should want to punch the perpetrators in the face.<br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> The thing that makes it hard to sympathise with the demonisation of the Get is that the exact moment they decided to fight harder is the moment the others abandoned them. They didn't try to reign the Get in, convince them there was a better way to fight, or offer to support, they seem to have gone 'lol, ur crazy, Gaia is dead, stop fighting'.<br /> <br /> I don't think whoever came up with the 'Gaia is dead' idea really thought through how a culture such as the Garou would react to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's one question to pose in response to that: If those are so important to W5, why haven't we heard about them till now? And I think we haven't because the worldbuilding you'd need to answer questions like that isn't part of W5.<br /> <br /> And the Get of Fenris are the bad guys because they exactly act like the warrior-Garou desperately trying to save Gaia you'd imagine. And Garou-culture is bad, though. And so they're a warning symbol to all other werewolves.<br /> <br /> Of course, the players are still supposed to fight the Wyrm and fight the good fight to save Gaia.<br /> <br /> And it doesn't have to make sense, of course. Does the local hunter cell / hunter org - division make sense after all? Is really everyone working for a hunter-organisation evil...? Or in the context of W5: Is everybody who wants to fight to save Gaia evil...?<br /> <br /> H5 didn't make sense, so why should W5?<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-10T17:19:13-08:00","id":1502718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502712#post1502712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we're to take the contempt that JA had for W:tA at face value, considering it was never in the cards, and having them just collapse in defeat was always the plan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sigh... &lt;usenet flashbacks intensifying&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T08:26:21-08:00","id":1502752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502718#post1502718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sigh... &lt;usenet flashbacks intensifying&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm kind of afraid to ask, but given his essay in the 2nd edition player's guide, I think I have an idea...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T13:15:38-08:00","id":1502767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502718#post1502718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sigh... &lt;usenet flashbacks intensifying&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't suppose anyone has any of this stuff archived or where I'd go looking?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 02-11-2023, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T15:27:44-08:00","id":1502778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502767#post1502767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't suppose anyone has any of this stuff archived or where I'd go looking?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's old archives for alt.games.whitewolf and alt.games.frp on google groups. Not all of it is there, but a lot is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T01:35:01-08:00","id":1502815,"title":"","content":"Yeah, theres not much remaining of the old white-wolf forums out there either, 95% of it isn't even findable through wayback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T09:24:44-08:00","id":1502841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502752#post1502752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm kind of afraid to ask, but given his essay in the 2nd edition player's guide, I think I have an idea...</div> </div> </div> </div>He was an edgelord who liked to provoke people and get into fights to show off how clever he was. Also when an argument went into a direction he didn't like it was always &quot;but we're the writers and you're not&quot;. There was a lot of drama with him and Deirdre Brooks in those days as they were very outspoken and available, and they were quite willing to engage in topics that people were grumpy about (i.e. discussions about the Avatar Storm or how Vampire is the only relevant gameline because it's the only culturally and financially significant one).<br /> <br /> Honestly, I am well aware that by reacing to emotions and memories I have from an ancient past I may be doing him some disservice. I will be the first to say that I've grown up a lot since then and that I was an idiot. I belive he did as well, and he spent a long time away from RPG's. The only thing that bugs me is that we're back having this whole street discussion and what's the &quot;right&quot; way to play games and it's rubbing me wrong and taking me back there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T13:20:40-08:00","id":1502870,"title":"","content":"His essay in the 2nd edition player's guide is also rather... charged, even if we set aside the language use of the time for the late 90s and its love of ableist r-slurs. Also, rather meandering in pointed comparison to all of Ethan Skemp's clearly and plainly presented things of importance in the game, which I believe we're mostly all looking back to fondly here if we had that book back in the day - things like &quot;no cosmic punishment, just the inevitable consequences of your own actions&quot; and &quot;nothing important sold over the counter&quot;. The former of those is in very stark contrast to Vampire's metaplot, which is practically nothing but cosmic punishments, right down to leaning hard into Noddism so the entire game is just one big cosmic punishment (and I guess its characters are suffering under one, too).<br /> <br /> W:tA has always been keenly aware of the stakes; we know that Gaia is at risk, thanks. There's only been a momentous prophecy about it since before any signs were evident - &quot;as things will be, but not as they should be&quot; and all. As I will constantly reiterate, the Umbra changing because of climate change isn't the way it does things - what likely would have instead is more of the frankly horrifying threats from Blood-Dimmed Tide getting uncomfortably closer to septs that formerly didn't think that they had to deal with them, and outright sinking caerns on islands or where there are other low-lying coastal areas, so that now the Garou have to negotiate for their use with the Rokea and Mokole on those Feras' own terms, which naturally requires most Garou to sit down and have a great big meal of humble pie, after they have to eat what the Corax pick out for them, to use a version of the phrase that the werecorvids wouldn't balk at.<br /> <br /> (And yes, I did choose that combination because I remembered <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=D65NFpo_GzM\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T13:40:11-08:00","id":1502874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502870#post1502870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">His essay in the 2nd edition player's guide is also rather... charged, even if we set aside the language use of the time for the late 90s and its love of ableist r-slurs. Also, rather meandering in pointed comparison to all of Ethan Skemp's clearly and plainly presented things of importance in the game, which I believe we're mostly all looking back to fondly here if we had that book back in the day - things like &quot;no cosmic punishment, just the inevitable consequences of your own actions&quot; and &quot;nothing important sold over the counter&quot;. The former of those is in very stark contrast to Vampire's metaplot, which is practically nothing but cosmic punishments, right down to leaning hard into Noddism so the entire game is just one big cosmic punishment (and I guess its characters are suffering under one, too).<br /> <br /> W:tA has always been keenly aware of the stakes; we know that Gaia is at risk, thanks. There's only been a momentous prophecy about it since before any signs were evident - &quot;as things will be, but not as they should be&quot; and all. As I will constantly reiterate, the Umbra changing because of climate change isn't the way it does things - what likely would have instead is more of the frankly horrifying threats from Blood-Dimmed Tide getting uncomfortably closer to septs that formerly didn't think that they had to deal with them, and outright sinking caerns on islands or where there are other low-lying coastal areas, so that now the Garou have to negotiate for their use with the Rokea and Mokole on those Feras' own terms, which naturally requires most Garou to sit down and have a great big meal of humble pie, after they have to eat what the Corax pick out for them, to use a version of the phrase that the werecorvids wouldn't balk at.<br /> <br /> (And yes, I did choose that combination because I remembered <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=D65NFpo_GzM\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I know exactly which one it is. the moment you mentioned it I took it down and read it again. Can I at least recommend Skemp's essay directly after that one as a palette cleanser?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T14:02:20-08:00","id":1502878,"title":"","content":"I just read that essay again... I mean, you just have to read the title and the last paragraph for actual useful information and the rest is just rambling. Although, there's some stuff in there that's eerily similar to his approach on W5. But really... this was based on bad gaming-experiences in the 90s... Talk about holding a grudge...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T15:04:16-08:00","id":1502881,"title":"","content":"Backtracking to the subject of &quot;If Gaia is inevitably going to die, what's the point of all this?&quot;, because it hits a thing that's bugged me on the tone of W5, but it's different from everyone else's, from what I've seen so far.<br /> <br /> Because Gaia was always fucked. The Garou were never going to win.<br /> <br /> People have always had a wide array of reactions to the game's embrace of the pre-millenial* apocalyptic fervor, but the end-of-the-world is one of those things that's baked into the games, the backbone of both the gothic and punk stylings. Hope had it's place, the possibliltiy of change had it's place, but World leaned more heavily into the punk reaction of retribution rather than a more gothic turn towards redemption, in that it's deafult understanding about the Apocalypse(and it's contemporaires) is that there's no real stopping it. Whether you liked that or not, it was there.<br /> <br /> So that being the case, why is it notably sour to hear the fact this way? And I know the answer, and that just makes it all the more bizarre how amateur the way it's handled here is.<br /> <br /> I mentioned in a rant about a fangame once that fatalism and nihilism are some of those themes you have to handle carefully for it to be rewarding, and the main way I came up with to do so was that the system (both in terms of setting and mechanics) had to strongly imply that everything would come to naught, but never directly say that that's the goal of the game outright. My suggestion at the time was that it used it's small scale failures that it was interested in be used to build up to a larger scale success, and then leave the success of those projects to speak for themselves (relying on the idea that no matter the ambition, the realization of such was never going to be enough to effect meaningfully trangressive change), and I've since made the argument that the way Beast: the Primordial handles that is also pretty clever, inviting you make something of yourself, your community, and your environment while allowing for the human flaws at work as well as the determined rejection of Heroes to strongly subtextually imply they'll never actually succeed, not in meaningful enough ways, all without never actually saying they can't or won't-in fact, it's got a very strong surface of Earn Your Happy Ending, even down to having explicit end goals that signify an arrival to success.<br /> <br /> In Apocalypse, the general way that it balances out that apocalyptic nihilism and fatalism with the validation and celebration of player action is by making the Garou good at battles and bad at wars. As a player character, you'll probably had lot of major successes alongside your myriad failures, lot of little campaigns and actions where you get to feel like you're making a difference, but when you step back and look at it from a top down perspective (often provided by the books on running examination, both just in general and through the metaplot) you can't help but shake the feeling those victories don't amount to anything for the grand problem. In fact, part of the reason the Apocalypse is inevitable is because so many of their powers-that-be over this have a top down power and influence on things even the whole Garou Nation can't match (though with how large both are, you could mistake otherwise), and that the damage done by those powers is already so much more than anything on the individual level can do about. I haven't read enough of Apocalypse to comment on how it balances this across the line, but in the initial presentations from the cores and what supplements I have, it does a really good job letting players focus on what they think they can do and the changes they can see, while letting storyteller's keep perspective on what it's <i>not</i> doing on the grand scale.<br /> <br /> The way W5 is going, though, with the Garou Nation beaten down and focused purely on the street level, basically doesn't allow the gameline the room to continue the sleight of hand. It makes it pretty naked that player involvement isn't going to win the war. There's no hypothetical of one set of allies taking something and building into something larger, until all these things done build up to a binding and cleansing of the Wyrm and a harmonious existence with nature is formed, because nothing's big enough anymore to create that illusion. It asks the question &quot;What are you going to do in the war against the Wyrm, knowing that anything you try is ultimately never going to be enough?&quot; rather than &quot;What are you going to do in the war against the Wyrm?&quot; and just relying on the Wyrm as the manifold manifestion of various forms of entropy (both built up over time and inevitable from the start) to be it's own statement, that you'll get the more you think about it.**<br /> <br /> And the fact that they made an error that is most readily comparable to a fangame's eager mistake is just kind of....disheartening.<br /> <br /> *because this means something related but different from how it's used nowadays, the turn of the millenium had an apocalyptic flavor all of it's own, and it's that sort of horror I'm talking about as opposed to the generation that got it assigned as a name alongside with the &quot;world continued with a whimper and a sigh&quot; ennui and new rights revolution furor they picked up.<br /> **And, because this is one of the strengths of letting the situation speak for itself, it also allows play groups to decide to reject that thesis, and decide just how much they want to, allowing for heroics in monstrosity with a thundering victory for a better world to Ragnarokian rebirths of a new world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-12-2023, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T15:38:07-08:00","id":1502884,"title":"","content":"The whole premise of W5 immediately falls apart upon examination:<ul><li>The Garou Nation has been torn apart: How? Why? Why am I still playing a Garou regardless?</li> <li>Gaia's dead/dying: How? Why? Is there a plan to do something about that?</li> <li>The setting's mid-Apocalypse: How? Why? And if everybody knows it's the middle of the Apocalypse where does the division in the Garou Nation come from?</li> </ul>This presentation may leave a lot of blanks but there's another concept called &quot;Actually the WOD is just our world...&quot;. Real-world-concepts will be brought in as stand-ins for antagonists and supporting characters. So there's that.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T16:00:41-08:00","id":1502886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502884#post1502884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole premise of W5 immediately falls apart upon examination:<ul><li>The Garou Nation has been torn apart: How? Why? Why am I still playing a Garou regardless?</li> <li>Gaia's dead/dying: How? Why? Is there a plan to do something about that?</li> <li>The setting's mid-Apocalypse: How? Why? And if everybody knows it's the middle of the Apocalypse where does the division in the Garou Nation come from?</li> </ul>This presentation may leave a lot of blanks but there's another concept called &quot;Actually the WOD is just our world...&quot;. Real-world-concepts will be brought in as stand-ins for antagonists and supporting characters. So there's that.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say that it falls apart, so much that it doesn't do a lot so far to make those playable. Playing with the order a bit:<ul><li>Gaia's dead?-okay, sell it on a setting to bring Gaia back to life, lots of media deals with revival and the costs of resurrection that can be tons of fun. You don't even need to make it possible, technically, just plant the idea that you <i>can</i> and let players run into the brick wall their own way.</li> <li>The Setting's Mid-Apocalypse?-okay, allow the overriding force of the Wyrm to let the setting get weirder and more unexpected-including ways that make it feasible to for bringing Gaia back, or creating a new world. Metrofinal, while predicated on more powerful actors, is a good example of how to pull off a story mid-apocalypse.</li> <li>The Garou's Nation's been torn apart? Cool, but what can be torn apart can be sewn together-the new tension is in how factions think that should be done, and how to take advantage of the new setting conceit and it's quirks.</li> </ul>All of those can be cool and fun quirks and conceits, and even keep in line with Apocalypse as a gameline (albeit, with limits). There is something particularly interesting in the question of what the sundered factions of a nation of predator-warriors do with the pursuit of global rebirth in the wake of an oncoming final death (hell, I'd love to see another gameline directly go into the idea). The current problem is that, instead of using these conceits as a foundation that will be built upon and expanded into interesting, plabyable ideas, they're simply presented <i>as</i> the playable ideas despites being conclusions on their own.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying these ideas <i>are </i>good, mind-but as anyone who works in creative fields can tell you, a bad idea executed well sells more than a great idea badly executed. Where this gets odd, again, is that I'm not sure if anyone is asking how they're going to make these things playable and fun. I'm sure they thought they could be those things, but I get the feeling no one did the homework to validate it, y'know?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T16:24:36-08:00","id":1502891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502881#post1502881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Apocalypse, the general way that it balances out that apocalyptic nihilism and fatalism with the validation and celebration of player action is by making the Garou good at battles and bad at wars. As a player character, you'll probably had lot of major successes alongside your myriad failures, lot of little campaigns and actions where you get to feel like you're making a difference, but when you step back and look at it from a top down perspective (often provided by the books on running examination, both just in general and through the metaplot) you can't help but shake the feeling those victories don't amount to anything for the grand problem. In fact, part of the reason the Apocalypse is inevitable is because so many of their powers-that-be over this have a top down power and influence on things even the whole Garou Nation can't match (though with how large both are, you could mistake otherwise), and that the damage done by those powers is already so much more than anything on the individual level can do about. I haven't read enough of Apocalypse to comment on how it balances this across the line, but in the initial presentations from the cores and what supplements I have, it does a really good job letting players focus on what they think they can do and the changes they can see, while letting storyteller's keep perspective on what it's <i>not</i> doing on the grand scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well basically W20 makes it pretty clear that most of the things what you is at best keeping the Status Quo but most likely only slowing down the inevitable. The reason for this is that with Pentex the servants of the wyrm made them so important, that the world became depandant on them. Garou could focus on killing wyrmspirits but this is just like killing the mobs that the boss regulary spawns but now having lost goal out of sight so the players can only try to stay alive.<br /> Going against Pentex just like this is useless to as now Pentex is keeping the body alive by feeding him slightly poisened food so they could stop the poisening but this would make the one that is going to be saved instead malnourished.<br /> So so far Garou would have only three real options.<br /> First either do a devil deal by allying with another super power that would be able to replace Pentex. That means either the vampires or the Technocracy and so accepting those as a trade for getting rid of Pentex corruption.<br /> Second would be going directly into Malfeas and so slaying one of the leaders of the wyrm which would be the personified corruption.<br /> Third one would be accepting the fault of the Garou too and so activly support the other changeing breeds and so becomeing only a part in the machine. Though this one is less likely as most Garou would argue this would come to late and so why even bothering.<br /> Maybe there would be a fourth way but this is the impression that W20 is giving you of why the war is getting lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T16:37:39-08:00","id":1502893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502886#post1502886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't say that it falls apart, so much that it doesn't do a lot so far to make those playable. Playing with the order a bit:<ul><li>Gaia's dead?-okay, sell it on a setting to bring Gaia back to life, lots of media deals with revival and the costs of resurrection that can be tons of fun. You don't even need to make it possible, technically, just plant the idea that you <i>can</i> and let players run into the brick wall their own way.</li> <li>The Setting's Mid-Apocalypse?-okay, allow the overriding force of the Wyrm to let the setting get weirder and more unexpected-including ways that make it feasible to for bringing Gaia back, or creating a new world. Metrofinal, while predicated on more powerful actors, is a good example of how to pull off a story mid-apocalypse.</li> <li>The Garou's Nation's been torn apart? Cool, but what can be torn apart can be sewn together-the new tension is in how factions think that should be done, and how to take advantage of the new setting conceit and it's quirks.</li> </ul>All of those can be cool and fun quirks and conceits, and even keep in line with Apocalypse as a gameline (albeit, with limits). There is something particularly interesting in the question of what the sundered factions of a nation of predator-warriors do with the pursuit of global rebirth in the wake of an oncoming final death (hell, I'd love to see another gameline directly go into the idea). The current problem is that, instead of using these conceits as a foundation that will be built upon and expanded into interesting, plabyable ideas, they're simply presented <i>as</i> the playable ideas despites being conclusions on their own.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying these ideas <i>are </i>good, mind-but as anyone who works in creative fields can tell you, a bad idea executed well sells more than a great idea badly executed. Where this gets odd, again, is that I'm not sure if anyone is asking how they're going to make these things playable and fun. I'm sure they thought they could be those things, but I get the feeling no one did the homework to validate it, y'know?</div> </div> </div> </div>Theoretically, none of this has to be bad. As you laid out the presentation in the previews is bad but I would add another factor to this which is H5. It's the Creative Lead's most recent work that he oversaw and wrote stuff for. And in the Introduction this was his pitch:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The ultimate Hunter intention in this regard is to get shit done. Unburdened by the ethically compromised agendas of the orgs, Hunter cells have the advantage of operating with an integrity and independence that the larger and more structured orgs can\u2019t.\u200b </div> </div> </div>As it says right there, local hunter-cells <i>can </i>show integrity and indepedence but H5 is all about acting like that's part of their nature and that's where the divide comes from. Hunter-orgs are <i>always </i>suspicious (because of their ulterior motives) and local hunter-cells are <i>always </i>paragons of integrity and righteousness. Because in H5's conception hunter-orgs ought to be demonized and there's no ambiguity left to give when it comes to local hunter-cells after that.<br /> <br /> And it doesn't make sense.<br /> <br /> The main-difference between local hunter-cells and hunter-orgs shouldn't be the moral character of the human hunters working for them, right? And yet, that's a focal point for H5. Somehow in terms of game-design the decision has been made to make it a focal point that hunters working in local cells are better people than the ones working for organizations... Why? Who knows... Supposedly, they're all just humans and yet...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T15:57:23-08:00","id":1502966,"title":"","content":"In fairness to W5 regarding the nihilism, I would rather the game lie to me poorly than lie to me well. At least then I can make a more informed decision vs. not fully understanding what I was committing to if I joined a game. If the actual stated premise of the game is supposed to be impossible to achieve in that game, I would rather know so I can just not waste my time working towards a cathartic victory that will never come. It's kind of nice that W5 is just so stark about its situation, since it allows me to just immediately realize what they're going for and that it's not for me.<br /> <br /> Like, if I was in a campaign and I ended up spending a substantial part of my earthly existence playing in it and then at the end the joke was &quot;haha fuck off, you can't fight fate, world ends, rox fall, everyone dies&quot;...that's the kind of shit friendships are broken over.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27305-joanna_crone","name":"Joanna_Crone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T01:46:16-08:00","id":1503117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joanna_Crone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502966#post1502966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, if I was in a campaign and I ended up spending a substantial part of my earthly existence playing in it and then at the end the joke was &quot;haha fuck off, you can't fight fate, world ends, rox fall, everyone dies&quot;...that's the kind of shit friendships are broken over.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> is wrong. Werewolf was never inherently nihilistic. Sure, the most likely outcome was failure for the simple scale of the problem you're dealing with and characters being human in their foibles. However, it was a game where the fight was worth it, and where trying to make the change mattered. To the point that it could actually change something and leave something better, even if it is not recognizable afterwards. Apocalypse (the book) itself goes quite deep into what might happen after and what different scenarios might be for the World and the Cosmos.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 02-15-2023, 05:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T01:58:13-08:00","id":1503118,"title":"","content":"As has been mentioned before, a lot of this can be simply averted by offering multiple modes of play in what way you want to tackle the game at your table and what you want to focus on. In addition, through ideas like &quot;The WOD is our world but darker&quot; and some more specific WtA-worldbuilding you also get some parameters/pointers for the setting/world and what you want to do with the game as you're playing it.<br /> <br /> With W5 Justin Achilli is rejecting all three of those things. There's only one mode of playing W5 (street-level with a focus on local conflicts), the WOD is &quot;just our world&quot; (so no more genre-storytelling and instead it's supposed to be more... realistic, I guess?) and 90% of the worldbuilding/lore has been thrown out, so the game doesn't give you any pointers on what to do with ideas like &quot;mid-apocalypse&quot; or &quot;Gaia's dead/dying&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T03:49:17-08:00","id":1503127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1503117#post1503117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> is wrong. Werewolf was never inherently nihilistic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Without getting into a big discussion about what exactly nihilism is (or which version of it we're actually talking about), what you're opposing is fatalism: that the apocalypse is coming and there's nothing you can do to stop it.<br /> <br /> Most forms of nihilism are actually strong counters to the impulse to be passive in a fatalistic situation. Since nihilism posits some or all of things you have preconceived to be important are not important, it liberates you to not be overwhelmed by the destruction at hand. If everything is only as important as we decide it is - nothing has an objective quality of importance - and all that matters is our personal desires, then success in the face of fatalism is imminently possible. The immediate and personal struggles in the face of calamity matter, because they matter to the people experiencing them in that moment, which is the only true source of meaning in the first pace. If losing the war is inevitable because the setting is fatalist, any value derived from choosing how you decided to go out is inherently (though not necessarily exclusively) a nihilistic impulse. <br /> <br /> The setting has consistently taken a nihilistic approach precisely because the stories that inspires in a fairly fatalistic setting. The impending fatalistic end is hard to tell stories about from other perspectives. Standing in front of the doom of the world, where Gaia, Luna, the Litany, the Nation, tradition, customs, and all of those external constraints are no longer shackled on you means you're free to say what you would do yourself without those pressures. A very compelling source of narrative drama.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T09:41:39-08:00","id":1503244,"title":"","content":"^What Heavy Arms said. THe setting assumes that, eventually, the Apocalypse will happen. WtA is a Ragnarok style story, which isn't surprising for a Gothic Punk RPG, because Ragnarok has a lot of the mood and feeling that Punk evokes.<br /> <br /> You may not like it, and you may not play it that way, but the games of World of Darkness are set before the End of All THings, and spends a lot of time not only establishing why that's the case and having that fact inform it's setting, but also basically explaining why it can't be avoided. It asks what you'll do with the coming of that good night, with a heavy exhortation to rage against the dying of the light.<br /> <br /> This is gothic punk-everything is dying, everything is falling apart, it's all their fault, and doesn't that just piss you off?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-16-2023, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T14:30:33-08:00","id":1503258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1503244#post1503244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">^What Heavy Arms said. THe setting assumes that, eventually, the Apocalypse will happen. WtA is a Ragnarok style story, which isn't surprising for a Gothic Punk RPG, because Ragnarok has a lot of the mood and feeling that Punk evokes.<br /> <br /> You may not like it, and you may not play it that way, but the games of World of Darkness are set before the End of All THings, and spends a lot of time not only establishing why that's the case and having that fact inform it's setting, but also basically explaining why it can't be avoided. It asks what you'll do with the coming of that good night, with a heavy exhortation to rage against the dying of the light.<br /> <br /> This is gothic punk-everything is dying, everything is falling apart, it's all their fault, and doesn't that just piss you off?</div> </div> </div> </div>Then again, we did get that Eighth Sign of the Phoenix in W20 that didn't seem to dismiss action as useless, but cathartic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T14:37:05-08:00","id":1503262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1503258#post1503258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then again, we did get that Eighth Sign of the Phoenix in W20 that didn't seem to dismiss action as useless, but cathartic.</div> </div> </div> </div>The two are not mutually exclusive, and just because the Apocalypse will happen doesn't mean the victories and the brief window in which they make things better are meaningless-unless, of course, that's how you want to take it.<br /> <br /> But, like. THe World is going to end, in universe. You have eight examples of that being the case. It's technically already happened! It very not technically always will! World of Darkness is set in the End of Days! Pre-apocalypse is baked into the setting and the genre! That's just a fact!<br /> <br /> People are, of course, free to ignore the text-but that doesn't mean they're suddenly right about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joanna_Crone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1502966#post1502966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fairness to W5 regarding the nihilism, I would rather the game lie to me poorly than lie to me well. At least then I can make a more informed decision vs. not fully understanding what I was committing to if I joined a game. If the actual stated premise of the game is supposed to be impossible to achieve in that game, I would rather know so I can just not waste my time working towards a cathartic victory that will never come. It's kind of nice that W5 is just so stark about its situation, since it allows me to just immediately realize what they're going for and that it's not for me.<br /> <br /> Like, if I was in a campaign and I ended up spending a substantial part of my earthly existence playing in it and then at the end the joke was &quot;haha fuck off, you can't fight fate, world ends, rox fall, everyone dies&quot;...that's the kind of shit friendships are broken over.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>If you've been enjoying the game so far, evidence suggests otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-16-2023, 06:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T16:31:05-08:00","id":1503276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1503244#post1503244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">^What Heavy Arms said. THe setting assumes that, eventually, the Apocalypse will happen. WtA is a Ragnarok style story, which isn't surprising for a Gothic Punk RPG, because Ragnarok has a lot of the mood and feeling that Punk evokes.<br /> <br /> You may not like it, and you may not play it that way, but the games of World of Darkness are set before the End of All THings, and spends a lot of time not only establishing why that's the case and having that fact inform it's setting, but also basically explaining why it can't be avoided. It asks what you'll do with the coming of that good night, with a heavy exhortation to rage against the dying of the light.<br /> <br /> This is gothic punk-everything is dying, everything is falling apart, it's all their fault, and doesn't that just piss you off?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage never was about the Apocalypse (except in the strictest Revalatory sense) until they shoehorned it in right at the tailend. Wraith was less about the End of All Things and more about how weird will it be the next time things change.<br /> <br /> And I may have misunderstood him, but what Heavy Arms has is that he challenged the terms being used. He posited that the situation is represented as fatalist, but that that does not mean that's the correct response to this, and that the game thrives on rebelling against that and refusing to accept it. And it's not like it's some kind of a hidden message or <i>&quot;being free to ignore the text&quot;</i>, it's there in the books - The odds are insane, you are fighting a cosmic principle gone mad, you are hobbled by a humanity gone haywire, by a nation of heroes that fucked up and alienated everyone and the world is most likely going to end. And yet, there are big changes, big fights and big damn heroes (in the classicist context).<br /> <br /> Revised, Apocalypse and the Prophecy of the Phoenix had shown us that there is hope and that what ever may happen there is something to fight for, and that all the sacrifice and attempts to make a change may lead to something positive. It may not, but you sure hell won't know if you don't get out there and DO SOMETHING.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T17:09:37-08:00","id":1503279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1503276#post1503276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Revised, Apocalypse and the Prophecy of the Phoenix had shown us that there is hope and that what ever may happen there is something to fight for, and that all the sacrifice and attempts to make a change may lead to something positive. It may not, but you sure hell won't know if you don't get out there and DO SOMETHING.</div> </div> </div> </div>In W20, the Eighth Phoenix Sign was going at that direction even more. There's hope, despite all the shitstorm that has happened, there's still hope. Fight for it, cherish it, nurture it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1876-fenixpp","name":"Fenixpp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T18:32:51-08:00","id":1503288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1503276#post1503276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mage never was about the Apocalypse (except in the strictest Revalatory sense) until they shoehorned it in right at the tailend. Wraith was less about the End of All Things and more about how weird will it be the next time things change.<br /> <br /> And I may have misunderstood him, but what Heavy Arms has is that he challenged the terms being used. He posited that the situation is represented as fatalist, but that that does not mean that's the correct response to this, and that the game thrives on rebelling against that and refusing to accept it. And it's not like it's some kind of a hidden message or <i>&quot;being free to ignore the text&quot;</i>, it's there in the books - The odds are insane, you are fighting a cosmic principle gone mad, you are hobbled by a humanity gone haywire, by a nation of heroes that fucked up and alienated everyone and the world is most likely going to end. And yet, there are big changes, big fights and big damn heroes (in the classicist context).<br /> <br /> Revised, Apocalypse and the Prophecy of the Phoenix had shown us that there is hope and that what ever may happen there is something to fight for, and that all the sacrifice and attempts to make a change may lead to something positive. It may not, but you sure hell won't know if you don't get out there and DO SOMETHING.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope you'll forgive me if I don't exactly trust the reading of someone who thought that Werewolf didn't have that much metaplot and said so to a writer whose job it was to compilate and summarize that metaplot for a book all about going over that metaplot. I hope you'll particularly forgive me when your understanding of Wraith's Oblivion somehow fails to account for how the Oblivion nakedly destroys the dead. I'm not the most read on World of Darkness(Mostly just the cores, usually for 2nd Editions when it comes up, of all the gamelines except Hunter and Mummy, and the 20th Anniversary Editions), but it doesn't take a whole lot before I start insisting you pull the other one.<br /> <br /> But yes, Apocalypse does say that you should rebel, it does say that you should fight, it says that standing against the Wyrm is a good and worthwhile thing to do.<br /> <br /> Does any of that change just because you won't win? Because if it does, then you don't value those things, you value <i><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1451877-test-case-the-anakim-and-the-victorious\">winning</a>, </i>and everything else is window dressing.<br /> <br /> The punk movement was all about destroying the machine, but punks of the time didn't really believe they could change governments or corporations. The forces they arrayed themselves against were just too big, and they openly acknowledged it, and still ran on the principle of throwing their bodies onto the gears of the machine to make it stop because a) they were still fucking pissed about governments and corporations fucking everything up, and b) because it was still good and worthwhile to stand against them.<br /> <br /> Gothic horror is often profoundly existential and concerned with the nature of humanity, and leans heavily into the romanticist notion that logic and reason could never hope to understand and tame the natural world, and the attempt was going to cost humanity more and more the further along it went, often with a fatalistic expectation. And yet, despite the feeling of inevitable decay that is at the heart of the genre, you still get victories. Dracula does, ultimately, get vanquished, as a brief example.<br /> <br /> Bringing it back to Apocalypse, the game gives you a cast of characters who could be unilaterally and succinctly understood as beings for whom the arts of destruction come particularly easy to...and ultimately pit them against the corrupted metaphysic of <i>destruction</i>.<br /> <br /> What did you think was going to happen? A war won and a happy ending? The master's house broken down by his own tools, the snake having devoured itself?<br /> <br /> But, and this is the big thing-does it really <i>matter</i>? For most people, the end of the world is just the backdrop, and what actually matters is what they do in the games. The characters don't know the world is for sure going to end-only players get to enjoy the tragic irony of that-and they very often tend to take more away from their character's victories than not.<br /> <br /> It's not Apocalypse specific, but one of my favorite gaming moments is from a series of games in World, where in the Storytellers and players <i>were</i> actively working towards a conclusion of the World ending. To make a long story as short as possible, continuing from a previous game, I had the goal of trying to cure another character's sister from being a Nephandi, but my character in the middle basically got eaten by a Technocratically enhanced corpse copy of my character who proceeded to have all of her experience and memory and hated every single second of it(it's complicated), and with promptly picking THAT up, had a character who was having a full on existential crises of who and what to be in the middle of a bunch of people who instantly regarded her as a monster and demon* and only managed to keep with the group by virtue of quick thinking and value-making. Once we were done with a) the war with the vampires and b) the battle with the Nephandi sister, my character was gonna have to part ways with the group.<br /> <br /> But it was this character who, after all the hate, mistrust, and angst and the HELL of going to battle with Baba Yaga's Hut in the Astral realm of Armageddon and then with the witch (long story) who, after biting the witch's head (not a long story, but long story) got the chance to put her to sleep and get a vampire to turn them, thus destroying the inverted Avatar and allowing the character a chance as one of the undead. WIth a character who took a -10 to the less than zero odds of pulling off that the original character had, I had done it. Against all odds, Sakura (Not-Kino) managed to save Gretel. Both are gonna need a shit ton of therapy from here, but it was still done.<br /> <br /> Do you think the fact that that was going to stop mattering just because we were going to end the world a few games later? Do think the fact the games have it baked in that the World of Darkness ends badly as rule at some indeterminate but soon point after any game that doesn't include the ending as part of it's gameplay? Hell, do you think the real world circumstances of basically never being able to finish that series of games and do more with Sakura and Gretel because that entire gaming group basically had a bad falling out with each other and I'm now burdened with how people who used to be my friends basically couldn't wait to get rid of me makes me smile less about having done that?<br /> <br /> Cause I tell you what, I still smile any time I think about that. I still get happy. Sakura saved Gretel. And then the world ended in the next two years.<br /> <br /> If thinking about the fact that the game is predicated on the fact that the Apocalypse will happen regardless of what you do sours your gaming experiences and shadows your thoughts of doing games in the future, I can't help you with that. But The Apocalypse is still inevitable in the books. I say again, the Apocalypse being inevitable <i>is text</i>. Not even particularly subtle or hidden.<br /> <br /> And Apocalypse, the game, still tells you that fighting it is meaningful, is valuable-hell, is <i>fun</i>. It follows the pattern set by Ragnarok-Ragnarok, where every god knows how they will ultimately fail and die, Ragnarok, where they never the less come to meet it because it is good and right that they should defy the inevitable, and even if not those is still a hell of a ride.<br /> <br /> Because the things that the Garou Nation are fighting for-messy, complicated, manifold, varied, odds-ended, squabbling, bickering things-aren't only worth it if they win the war.<br /> <br /> If anything, they're all the more valuable because they'll always <i>lose</i>. But more importantly, they're worth fighting for because <i>they are worth fighting for</i>.<br /> <br /> Everything else is a matter of what you think is worth losing for.**<br /> <br /> *unrelated but fun tangent, at some point in the shenanigans, we went up against a Nephandi Celestial Chorister for [reasons] who cast a hellfire spell that basically would have killed my character if it connected. The Storyteller gave me a chance to come up with some kind of a Hail Mary, and after a bit I went &quot;Well, it stands to reason you wouldn't expect Hellfire to really hurt a demon, yeah?And people have been thinking of and describing my character as a demon this whole damn time, right? Great, I'mma take that sympathetic connection and empower it to hell and back,&quot; and managed to roll basically a shit ton of successes for it, and thus survived by semantic semitoic fuckery. It's probably bullshit for how the actual metaphysics work, but I felt like I had caught the damn roadrunner with that one.<br /> **But maybe don't play a game predicated on the end of the world if you can't accept it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-16-2023, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T19:25:39-08:00","id":1503295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1503244#post1503244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may not like it, and you may not play it that way, but the games of World of Darkness are set before the End of All THings, and spends a lot of time not only establishing why that's the case and having that fact inform it's setting, but also basically explaining why it can't be avoided. It asks what you'll do with the coming of that good night, with a heavy exhortation to rage against the dying of the light.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth noting that in the Asian werewolf setting (Hengeyokai) the core concept is the Wheel of Ages, which is a bit less fatalistic than what you have the rest of the Werewolf setting. The 1st Age was great, but things slowly got worse over time as the Wheel turned through the 1st, 2nd, 3rd, 4th and 5th Ages. The 6th Age is going to be horrific, but it's not going to be The End. Once the Sixth Age passes, the wheel will keep turning and things will begin getting better. This is even a central conceit of the Devil Tiger splat from Kindred of the East - they plan to burn themselves out during the Sixth Age, forcing the wheel to start turning faster, so that ideally the Sixth Age will only last a few months or years at the most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T22:25:20-08:00","id":1503306,"title":"","content":"Throughout all of human history a not insignificant amount of people held a belief along the lines of &quot;the earth is immeasurably old but the end is somehow nigh&quot;. Also popular is the idea that the earliest age and it's people were great, the next age was good, the age before now was ok, and the todays suck. Garou are pretty extreme in this regard. But you could argue the real world is making great progress. Since the WoD really revolves around human folly, some kind of cosmic horror would be a buzzkill, especially if it was just related to one splat's particular field and humanity never had any idea of spirits, and so the world should only end when humans end it at least enough for us to turn our cities into bunkers (or it actually ends, but we won't be much around to really debate that) <br /> <br /> And the (happy for us, sad for the setting) is that a lot of things we feared aren't so big or are being dealt with quite well. As much as the normalization of nuclear war would be a horror show, modern nukes are smaller and more accurate than older models and with some degree of disarmament we no longer really have the capacity to destroy the world 12 times over. And while the developing world is growing rapidly and going to be polluting they also have a lot of hindsight/late adopter/outside influence to avoid the worst of it. I'm more worried about automation, a widening gap between rich and poor, wages not covering prices, automated policing, and having to rent my kids to billionaires so that we can eat; but I don't think that's the apocalypse Garou have in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-17T06:56:41-08:00","id":1503314,"title":"","content":"We've also seen some great successes on the environmental front since the 90's. Back then the hole in the Ozone layer was a huge deal. These days? Nobody talks about it because the laws and regulations that were passed have let it heal up. Or acid rain was all over the news, but again, you saw legislation to improve automobiles and factory emissions and these days, acid rain is one of those things that many younger people might not have even heard of. <br /> <br /> Of course there's still problems like Global Warming, or pollution causing mass extinction events, or the Great Pacific Garbage patch. But it's hard for me to be <i>too</i> fatalistic when we've seen some very recent examples of humans successfully taking steps to solve major environmental issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-17T09:29:32-08:00","id":1503324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1503314#post1503314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've also seen some great successes on the environmental front since the 90's. Back then the hole in the Ozone layer was a huge deal. These days? Nobody talks about it because the laws and regulations that were passed have let it heal up. Or acid rain was all over the news, but again, you saw legislation to improve automobiles and factory emissions and these days, acid rain is one of those things that many younger people might not have even heard of.<br /> <br /> Of course there's still problems like Global Warming, or pollution causing mass extinction events, or the Great Pacific Garbage patch. But it's hard for me to be <i>too</i> fatalistic when we've seen some very recent examples of humans successfully taking steps to solve major environmental issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which, ironically for this board, is why you really don't actually want to present ecological issues as &quot;the apocalypse&quot;. Because efforts can make a difference, and the prospective &quot;end&quot; can be averted. Also, because a major roadblock to accomplishing this, at least in US politics and maybe a few other places, are denominations of Christianity that do believe that the end is night and accordingly that trying to preserve the world is either doomed or somehow actively evil. (Next up on the problem list from the same place, of course, is the &quot;God wouldn't let it happen&quot; crowd, but that's technically a different problem).<br /> <br /> So, now that I've kind of just argued that the game shouldn't exist, I need to go contemplate on how to get the punk anger without titling something after an eschatological event.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-17T10:19:41-08:00","id":1503327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1503288#post1503288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope you'll forgive me if I don't exactly trust the reading of someone who thought that Werewolf didn't have that much metaplot and said so to a writer whose job it was to compilate and summarize that metaplot for a book all about going over that metaplot. I hope you'll particularly forgive me when your understanding of Wraith's Oblivion somehow fails to account for how the Oblivion nakedly destroys the dead. I'm not the most read on World of Darkness(Mostly just the cores, usually for 2nd Editions when it comes up, of all the gamelines except Hunter and Mummy, and the 20th Anniversary Editions), but it doesn't take a whole lot before I start insisting you pull the other one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no worries there, no forgiveness for the disingenuous. Since you're dragging multiple things out of context, let's go in order.<br /> <br /> Michele did an amazing job at collecting the collective history of WtA and I even have the final pages of Apocalyptic record printed out and inserted into my copy of Apocalypse so I can have a quick reference for my own library. What I said, and what I still stand behind is that when people judge metaplot they judge it by Vampire's yardstick - harsh, unforgiving changes removing whole factions, playstyles and mechanics while showing up how awesome NPC's are compared to the PC's, that will never ever matter. Werewolf was not only burdened by much less metaplot, but actually bothered to make it metaplot that introduced new things and opened up a lot of ways for PC's to be a part of it. The First is something people bemoan metaplot, the second is something that people tend to miss about the metaplot.<br /> <br /> Wraith is a game about being unable to let go because of fear and human foibles. It's core social interaction is based on ageless, deathless relics of lost times desperately hanging on not to lose who they are to the everpresent Oblivion. Which is probably the ultimate irony of the game because:<br /> <br /> A) Oblivion is not the only way out<br /> B) Being unable to let go is what got them here in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1503288#post1503288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bringing it back to Apocalypse, the game gives you a cast of characters who could be unilaterally and succinctly understood as beings for whom the arts of destruction come particularly easy to...and ultimately pit them against the corrupted metaphysic of <i>destruction</i>.<br /> <br /> What did you think was going to happen? A war won and a happy ending? The master's house broken down by his own tools, the snake having devoured itself?<br /> <br /> But, and this is the big thing-does it really <i>matter</i>? For most people, the end of the world is just the backdrop, and what actually matters is what they do in the games. The characters don't know the world is for sure going to end-only players get to enjoy the tragic irony of that-and they very often tend to take more away from their character's victories than not.<br /> <br /> If thinking about the fact that the game is predicated on the fact that the Apocalypse will happen regardless of what you do sours your gaming experiences and shadows your thoughts of doing games in the future, I can't help you with that. But The Apocalypse is still inevitable in the books. I say again, the Apocalypse being inevitable <i>is text</i>. Not even particularly subtle or hidden.<br /> <br /> And Apocalypse, the game, still tells you that fighting it is meaningful, is valuable-hell, is <i>fun</i>. It follows the pattern set by Ragnarok-Ragnarok, where every god knows how they will ultimately fail and die, Ragnarok, where they never the less come to meet it because it is good and right that they should defy the inevitable, and even if not those is still a hell of a ride.<br /> <br /> Because the things that the Garou Nation are fighting for-messy, complicated, manifold, varied, odds-ended, squabbling, bickering things-aren't only worth it if they win the war.<br /> <br /> If anything, they're all the more valuable because they'll always <i>lose</i>. But more importantly, they're worth fighting for because <i>they are worth fighting for</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>And here you go putting words in my mouth, again. I never said the Apocalypse is not going to happen. However, what it is, how it will go down, who will be there, why they will be there, what will be left is quite open, to the point that there is a whole discussion on that in the actual Apocalypse book. And this is a positive thing, one predicated on people going out and doing things and trying to be better. And whatever happens, it will be legendary.<br /> <br /> Which is quite opposite to the whole &quot;We lost, now let's eke out an existence in the smallscale ashes of the world counting it's last days&quot; that W5 is currently pitching.<br /> <br /> And that's the main reason the whole &quot;oh the game's lying to you&quot; sentiment, really, really bugs me. For 9 out of 10 games it surely won't matter, but actually going into the game and thinking &quot;oh a shame they died saving the last Glade Child it will amount to nothing&quot; doesn't sound like a fun headspace to actually be writing stories from - or judging them from a meta-contextual point as a player.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1503288#post1503288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything else is a matter of what you think is worth losing for.**<br /> <br /> **But maybe don't play a game predicated on the end of the world if you can't accept it.</div> </div> </div> </div>But maybe be less condescending.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T00:15:06-08:00","id":1503359,"title":"","content":"Paradox just needs to cancel W5","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T00:59:31-08:00","id":1503361,"title":"","content":"At this point... I'm not sure that's really the case. It's not like they can get a tax write off for it or something. They have it. Supposedly it's basically done. There are lots of people that are still going to buy it. They do need to see the WoD books make more money. <br /> <br /> If anything it coming out and bombing hard might actually be a kick in their pants to reevaluate what they're doing. Cancelling it wouldn't have that impact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T15:22:15-08:00","id":1503402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1503361#post1503361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At this point... I'm not sure that's really the case. It's not like they can get a tax write off for it or something. They have it. Supposedly it's basically done. There are lots of people that are still going to buy it. They do need to see the WoD books make more money.<br /> <br /> If anything it coming out and bombing hard might actually be a kick in their pants to reevaluate what they're doing. Cancelling it wouldn't have that impact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah it is what it is. Their book schedule is sparse and they need something. I'm sure there will be enough buzz about &quot;new version of classic rpg!&quot;. How much it sells beyond that will depend on a number of factors. I'm really, really curious about sales of HtR5, but it's hard to get those numbers. Best I could do is with the comparative thing I did with Amazon sales, but that's lacking the hobby (web)stores.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T16:47:47-08:00","id":1503409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1503361#post1503361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At this point... I'm not sure that's really the case. It's not like they can get a tax write off for it or something. They have it. Supposedly it's basically done. There are lots of people that are still going to buy it. They do need to see the WoD books make more money.<br /> <br /> If anything it coming out and bombing hard might actually be a kick in their pants to reevaluate what they're doing. Cancelling it wouldn't have that impact.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, one thing that actually might hurt them there is the pricing Renegade Publishing goes for... H5 was 40 bucks for the pdf. With W5 being a bigger book and inflation... maybe it will be even more...<br /> <br /> The focus is on physical sales working out, it feels like. There's also this program of tying early-access-pdfs to you ordering physical copied when it comes to the V5 players guide and the first H5 supplement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T19:36:51-08:00","id":1503419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1503409#post1503409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">h5 was 40 bucks for the pdf</div> </div> </div> </div>h5 was 40 bucks pdf?<br /> <br /> Lol","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T22:48:04-08:00","id":1503426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1503419#post1503419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> h5 was 40 bucks pdf?<br /> <br /> Lol</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the proverbial gun to the head of prospective buyers to get them to buy the physical book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T23:46:06-08:00","id":1503428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502344-gnosis-being-removed-being-relegated-to-renown-in-w5?p=1503361#post1503361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At this point... I'm not sure that's really the case. It's not like they can get a tax write off for it or something. They have it. Supposedly it's basically done. There are lots of people that are still going to buy it. They do need to see the WoD books make more money.<br /> <br /> If anything it coming out and bombing hard might actually be a kick in their pants to reevaluate what they're doing. Cancelling it wouldn't have that impact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that's partly why I want it to come out. I think it might be a splash of water to the face if it undersells","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T08:48:05-08:00","id":1503453,"title":"","content":"Of course, how big of a splash depends on their internal projections more than our external attempts to gauge things.<br /> <br /> For example, we as WoD fans, have a strong preconception that Werewolf should sell better than Hunter; at least on the TT RPG side of things. WtA was a much bigger brand than Hunter until the HtR video games, and within the fan community was generally seen as a more important aspect of what makes the WoD the WoD.<br /> <br /> But if you put a lot of that aside and think critically about it.. that's a lot of assumptions that are based far more in the realities of 2000 than 2023. Emotionally I might balk at the idea of W5 selling as well as H5 being a &quot;success,&quot; I can't logic up a reason for why Paradox would be wrong to set that as a metric if they're happy with H5 setting the baseline for future WoD5 non-VtM book sales.<br /> <br /> While a lot of us would consider W5 doing at least as well as H5 to be a gigantic red flag that things are going bad with WoD5, we're not Paradox's bean counters. If their internal goal is &quot;do at least as well as H5,&quot; they could hit that even with a lot of negative perceptions in the fandoms that this isn't good enough for WtA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 02-19-2023, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T11:43:26-08:00","id":1503467,"title":"","content":"Considering the mess that the whole Paradox/WOD5E-affair has been thus far, I can easily picture Paradox just being satisfied by the mere fact that W5 will come out and can be bought.<br /> <br /> Then again, just after settling into this new arrangement with the WOD-team and Renegade, things are getting complicated again because Justin Achilli, the Creative Lead, has left.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}